# Shared Game Constants

Shared numeric/vector tuning lives in `src/ReplicatedStorage/Components/Common/GameProperties.luau`. Module-private values stay `local`. Complex tables belong in Data/templates, not here.

Put in GameProperties: gameplay math, limits, sizes, speeds, angles, shared timing / rate-limit / grid config. Style: `Data.NAME = value`, `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`, optional unit comment (`-- studs`), `TableUtil.Lock(Data)`.

```luau
-- ❌ local magic number in a feature script
local MOVE_SPEED = 50

-- ✅ GameProperties.luau
Data.BUILD_CAM_MOVEMENT_SPEED = 50 -- studs/s
```

After requiring it, alias used props under `-- CONSTANTS` and use the locals — don't repeat `GameProperties.*` in logic. Skip the alias only for a true one-off. Don't rewrite existing inline reads (e.g. server TycoonController rate limits) unless you're already editing that code.

Do **not** put in GameProperties: instances, services, OOP/module state, or one-off values that aren't tuning.
